The Perl port treats JSON that is no object as no input and only takes a non-empty string cwd (Skilletor::CLI::_hook_input, Skilletor::Hooks::_text).

Reproduce with a TS test, fix in hooks.ts/cli.ts (input that is not an object = {}; cwd only when a non-empty string), then pin it with a conformance hook case so both CLIs agree. Exit stays 0 either way (spec §8).

